---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ChapterHero from '../components/ChapterHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Cub Scout Pack 170’s local unit website handles parent inquiries, youth information, photographs, and third-party links."
>
  <ChapterHero
    chapter="Site policy"
    title="Privacy for"
    accent="Pack 170 families"
    intro="This policy applies to macon170.com, a local unit website. It is separate from Scouting America’s and the Central Georgia Council’s privacy policies."
    noteTitle="Policy status"
    noteBody="In effect"><p slot="note">Last reviewed: July 2026.</p></ChapterHero
  >
  <section class="section">
    <article class="container paper-sheet policy">
      <h2>Who this site serves</h2><p>
        This website shares public information with parents, guardians, and community members. It is not directed to children for the
        purpose of collecting personal information. A parent or guardian should submit every inquiry.
      </p><h2>Information a parent provides</h2><p>
        The contact form collects a parent or guardian’s name, email address, selected topic, and message. A parent may optionally provide
        their phone number and their child’s grade. Do not submit a child’s name, home address, school, phone number, medical information,
        or other sensitive details.
      </p><h2>How inquiries are handled</h2><p>
        Parent inquiries should route to multiple authorized adult pack volunteers. The site does not create direct or private adult–youth
        messaging. Information is used to respond to the inquiry and support the family’s participation in the pack.
      </p><h2>Youth names and photographs</h2><p>
        If youth are identified publicly, the site will use first name and last initial at most. Pack photographs will only be published
        when the pack has the required permission and has checked current opt-outs. Event-level captions are preferred over naming
        individual youth.
      </p><h2>Public site</h2><p>
        Everything on this website is public. The site does not provide a members-only area, private group, direct messaging, or youth
        account.
      </p><h2>Storage, security, and service providers</h2><p>
        Contact submissions are stored in Cloudflare D1. Cloudflare Turnstile checks whether a submission appears automated, and Cloudflare
        Access authenticates allowlisted volunteers before they can open the volunteer desk. Basic security metadata may include submission
        time, browser user-agent, country code, and Turnstile verification details. The pack does not intentionally store the visitor’s IP
        address in D1.
      </p><h2>Third-party links</h2><p>
        The site may link to BeAScout, the Central Georgia Council, Highland Hills Baptist Church, and other services selected by Pack 170
        adults. Those services have their own privacy practices. No analytics service is currently configured; this policy must be updated
        before one is enabled.
      </p><h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>
        Contact submissions and their volunteer audit records are automatically deleted after 365 days. Pack leadership may delete
        information sooner when it is no longer needed for the inquiry, pack administration, safety, or applicable recordkeeping. A parent
        may request review or deletion through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p><h2>Changes</h2><p>
        The effective or review date shown above will change when this policy materially changes. Pack 170 adults should review this policy
        whenever forms, analytics, photography practices, or administrators change.
      </p><h2>Contact</h2><p>
        Pack 170 does not publish adult email addresses. Send every question about this site or this policy through the{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>; it reaches multiple authorized adult volunteers.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .policy {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    max-width: 82ch;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-top: 2.8rem;
  }
  .policy .notice {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
